  "text": "An aisling is a poem, a vision or a dream. It is a form of Irish verse. The best known poem is the Aislinge Óengusa, the vision of Aonghus, about the love of that god for the swan maiden Cáer. Another old poem is the Aislinge Meic Con Glinne, the vision of Mac Conglinne. Many later aislings were poems of the land. In them the poet meets the goddess of Sovereignty, alone and ruined.",
